1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,587
Your onion shoots tiny

2
00:00:01,587 --> 00:00:03,095
droplets when you cut
it.

3
00:00:03,695 --> 00:00:06,008
One lab caught it on
cameras far

4
00:00:06,008 --> 00:00:08,110
faster than your eyes
can see.

5
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:10,228
Droplets burst out at

6
00:00:10,228 --> 00:00:12,503
up to about ninety miles
an hour.

7
00:00:13,203 --> 00:00:15,244
That was a lab rig that
drops

8
00:00:15,244 --> 00:00:17,897
a blade onto half an
onion, not a chef.

9
00:00:18,497 --> 00:00:20,474
Within a fiftieth of a
second,

10
00:00:20,474 --> 00:00:23,153
they split into hundreds
of smaller drops.

11
00:00:23,753 --> 00:00:24,796
Why cry?

12
00:00:24,796 --> 00:00:26,656
Cutting breaks open the
cells.

13
00:00:26,656 --> 00:00:29,441
A reaction turns the
onion's sulfur

14
00:00:29,441 --> 00:00:31,839
compounds into an eye
irritant.

15
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:34,777
It switches on nerves in
your cornea,

16
00:00:34,777 --> 00:00:36,640
the clear front of your
eye.

17
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,344
Tears.

18
00:00:38,244 --> 00:00:40,511
One chemist suggested
the droplets

19
00:00:40,511 --> 00:00:42,648
carry that irritant to
your eyes.

20
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:45,912
The thin, tough skin on
each layer lets

21
00:00:45,912 --> 00:00:48,582
the flesh under it get
squeezed first.

22
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:49,637
Then it bursts.

23
00:00:50,337 --> 00:00:52,280
A blunter knife makes it
worse.

24
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,626
So do faster cuts.

25
00:00:54,226 --> 00:00:57,271
A sharper blade gave
fewer, slower droplets.

26
00:00:58,171 --> 00:01:00,961
But the team tracked
droplets, not tears.

27
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:03,822
And it's one study, in
one lab.

28
00:01:04,422 --> 00:01:07,186
The Pan Theory: sharpen
your knife tonight.

29
00:01:07,186 --> 00:01:09,792
Fewer droplets, and
maybe fewer tears.

